{# Widget "plan" — Planned vs actual (PL·19), off by default; the "The month
   ahead" direction turns it on.

   HELD — the model records no plan. "Planned vs actual" compares what was meant
   to happen each week against what was walked, and this module holds only the
   walked side (the "Patrols per week" chart). There is no planning entity: a
   patrol is created when it starts or is imported, never scheduled ahead. A plan
   is a roster, which the future Operations module owns; when it ships, this
   widget reads it and the dashed "planned" bars appear beside the solid "walked"
   ones. Until then the card says what it cannot yet compare, rather than drawing
   a plan nobody entered. #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Planned vs actual<span class="src">· {{ (month|default(now))|date('F Y')|lower }} · by week</span></span>
    <p class="patrol-empty">This module records what was walked, not what was planned — so there is nothing yet to compare against. Planning a patrol ahead is the future <b>Operations</b> module’s; when it ships, each week’s plan appears here beside what was actually walked. The walked side is already on the <b>Patrols per week</b> chart.</p>
</div>
